#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SD0022 expect=violation domain=AE
#note "The merged M11 sister (one sister per (target variable, package)), FDA-SD0022 branch: none of AESTDTC/AESTRF/AESTRTPT is present (None satisfied), the exemption columns AEOCCUR/AESTAT are absent (R-5.22: --OCCUR != 'N' fires on a missing value; empty(--STAT) true), and AEENDTC exists but is BLANK, pinning that the FDA-SD0031 branch of the union trigger contributes nothing here. Sensitivity is Dataset: reported ONCE although both rows qualify. Same dataset shape as the parent's skipped_no_start_columns scenario."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 1
dataset AE class=EVENTS label="Adverse Events"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col AESEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col AETERM  type=Char label="Reported Term for the Adverse Event"
col AEENDTC type=Char label="End Date/Time of Adverse Event"
---
S1 | AE | 001 | 1 | HEADACHE |
S1 | AE | 001 | 2 | NAUSEA   |
